<!--
Magnetic pod carrying archives and files (corona): a futuristic passenger/goods car for the fast transport of files and data between the sectors of the corona.
Written by Gemini CLI (Gemini 3.8 Flash, subscription), task T50a.
Box: 2.5 × 1 × 1.25 tiles, 20 × 8 × 10 voxels, 8 voxels per tile (vpt: 8).
Role: prop.
Design and sculptural concept:
- A torpedo/magnetic bullet car, aerodynamic and tapered, for high speed along the X axis;
- A futuristic two-tone body: lower shell in ultra-dark carbon composite (M, m) and roof/shoulders in satin titanium and chrome (S, s);
- Magnetic repulsion suspension: it travels visibly raised 1 voxel off the ground, anchored at z=0 by two bogies (front and back) with anti-friction pads (P) and magenta neon blade repulsion coils (R, r, A, glow="True") casting a glowing trail on the ground;
- A central levitating air-span section (x=7..12) fully suspended over the void at z=0 with a ventral magnetic beam;
- Darkened, mirrored panoramic windows with cyan-blue posts (V, v) and open housings through which the data capsules shine;
- Lit archive interiors: through the side and the windows one glimpses neat stacks of shining quantum data cubes (1, 2, 3, 4, G, glow="True") and a central floating holographic core;
- A tapered nose with double white laser beam headlights (W, glow="True") and a cyan lidar telemetry scanner (C, glow="True");
- A tapered torpedo tail with double magenta vectored plasma thruster nozzles (T, t, glow="True"), cobalt position lights (c, glow="True") and a swept-back finned dorsal fin in chrome (s);
- A low-profile aerodynamic spine with a high-frequency data radome and a cyan navigation beacon (C).
Animation "levitazione" (4 frames):
- The magnetic pads pulse, modulating the induction and sending a magenta repulsion wave along (R -> r -> A);
- The inner data archives cycle the quantum energy of the files in transit synchronisation (1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4);
- The thrusters and the route telemetry pulse in sequence (T -> t, C -> c).
-->
